                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Found the game fun so wanted to give some Positive love for a new release. \n\nIf this is your genre of game, its probably a piece of cake. If not, there is a small challenge initially while you adapt your brain and hand-eye coordination to ignore the constantly changing orientation. [spoiler]Always move up and down regardless of what you see. [/spoiler]\n\nFor achievement seekers if you are into this kind of game or awesome at all genres it should be a quick. Otherwise just a little more effort while you train the muscle memory to respond. \n\nThe achievement that would require the most effort (due to real time) is accumulating 10k and 50k parsec (distance traveled). \nUpdate:\nThe Dev has eluded it could be a bug or just genius but as long as you keep the game open the parsec will not reset allowing you to accumulate both 10 and 50k parsec from multiple runs. \n[i]Topic here: http://steamcommunity.com/app/410470/discussions/0/485624040227066354/[/i]",
